whether you're into first person or  third person 2023 is looking to be  another great year for the shooter genre  here are 19 of the biggest ones that are  set to release this year  these first two games are XBox exclusive  day one game pass releases that have had  quite a bit of Buzz around them  Starfield and redfall they are also the  first two on the list that do not have a  solid release date but are still  confirmed for some time in 2023 as of  this video's recording Starfield is the  next epic adventure from Bethesda and  it's the developer's first new IP in  over 20 years the game's director Todd  Howard has described it as more of a  hardcore RPG than the Studio's previous  works but based on the Combat gameplay  we've seen so far shooting is still a  big part of the game those RPG elements  come into play in The Game's impressive  character creator that features a wide  variety of backgrounds and traits the  character you play as will also have  their own unique set of talents and  flaws based on the choices you make  around the Galaxy Howard also confirmed  players will be able to visit over 1 000  planets some will be full-fledged cities  While others will be procedurally  generated we still don't know much about  starfield's main campaign but we do know  things like it will be set in the year  2330 during a time in which humans have  mastered space travel and live in an  area of the solar system referred to as  the settled systems you play as the  space fairer after receiving an  invitation to join the constellation aka  the group of last Space Explorers who  are committed to unlocking the mysteries  of the Galaxy redfall on the other hand  takes place on Earth in the fictional  island town of redfall Massachusetts  this one sweet Community has become  overrun with vampires and a cult that  worships them now it's up to you and  your crew of survivors to find a way out  this group consists of cryptozoologist  and inventor devinder crowsley combat  engineer Remy De la Rosa ex-military  Sharpshooter Jacob Boyer and biomedical  engineering student Leila Ellison  redfall will have a linear campaigns set  within an open world filled with  optional side quests and environmental  storytelling borrowing elements from  previous Arcane games like Dishonored  and prey redfall will feature stealth  and immersive Sim elements however  unlike those games we're using the  environment to your advantage and  stealth mechanics are encouraged redfall  if the trailers are any indication seems  to swing a bit towards action-focused  combat but as awesome as those games  look let's talk about two games that you  can play sooner in February you'll have  atomic heart on the 21st and Destiny 2  lightfall a week later on the 28th  lightfall is the year 6 expansion for  Destiny 2 that features a new story set  on the neon cyberpunk city of Neo Muno  on planet Neptune where people who  escape the collapse created a metropolis  over the past centuries without the last  City knowing lightfall will include new  enemies and allies another Darkness  subclass called strand and updated  in-game features in an effort to help  New Destiny 2 players transition from  New Light missions into the rest of the  content Bungie is introducing Guardian  ranks this is a knowledge ladder where  players can progress through different  ranks that guide them through the game  according to the game's director Joe  Blackburn lightfall is quote the  beginning of the end of the light and  darkness Saga and for those of you that  have been following the story for some  time it's a big deal atomic heart drops  a week before lightfall which might give  you just enough time to beat it before  jumping back into the destiny 2 raid  grind I think good luck with that atomic  heart is a first person shooter that  takes place in an alternative reality  1955 the USSR defeated Nazi Germany  thanks to advances in robotics and now  the Soviet Union is using that Tech to  make everyday life easier that is until  the AI turns on humans just like it will  eventually in real life damn it a  computer definitely really hurt that the  gameplay of atomic heart has you firing  weapons with one hand and Supernatural  Powers with the other and true Bioshock  fashion in March you can look forward to  exploring the world of the day before an  open world MMO Survival game set in a  post-pandemic America the undead are  everywhere and the humans that are left  have become so desperate for survival  they're willing to kill almost anyone  for resources the entire package looks  like a cross between the last of us and  the division so fans looking forward to  the division Heartland a free-to-play  spin-off can get lost in the day before  while they wait for new information from  Ubisoft the only limitation to the day  before is it's only releasing on PC  sorry console fam the game also is  sitting at the number two spot for the  most wishlist of games on Steam at the  time of this recording so the hype seems  pretty real and if that isn't enough  zombies for you don't worry Dead Island  2 has you covered and will release on  April 28th this sequel which was  originally announced in 2014 does not  seem to Veer too far away from what the  first game was like it's a first person  open world RPG set in a zombie infested  Los Angeles that leans into over-the-top  combat characters and crafted weapons  players will take on the role of six  different characters with a respect  system that is meant to be used often  and easily to give players access to  many ever-changing character builds you  can even get bitten and harness the  power of a zombie which sounds cool and  scary all at the same time oh and by the  way no you're not crazy Los Angeles is  not on an island but let's keep this  survival theme going for one more game  because stalker 2 heart of Chernobyl is  coming out this year as well stalker 2  is the long-awaited mainline sequel to  the cult classic original stalker shadow  of Chernobyl from 2007 a PC exclusive  back then the game spawned two  follow-ups in quick succession first in  2008 and then one in 2009 stalker 2 will  see players once again taking on the  role of a gas mask wearing rat munching  Survivor in and around Chernobyl  exclusion Zone the site of the infamous  1986 catastrophe that has caused  suffering for generations of people who  were exposed to the nuclear reactors  effects the monsters and factions inside  of the Zone will interact with each  other in a simulated living world and  the studio claims events will be  happening constantly whether or not  you're there to witness them it also  promises a branching story with loads of  different endings based on your choices  and that its open world will be one of  the biggest to date if you're looking  for more ways to spend time with your  friends check out hyenas exoprimal or  payday 3. hyenas is a team-based and  class-based extraction Royale of sorts  from creative assembly that tasks  players with robbing high-tech vaults on  massive space Freighters sometimes in  zero gravity each match has 15 play  players split into three teams of five  and the loot you'll be stealing includes  pop culture themed artifacts the game  will be releasing on Xbox series X Xbox  One PlayStation 4 and 5 and PC and the  release window is set for some time in  2023. EXO Primal is a team-based  multiplayer game that has you running  around in mechanical Mech suits fighting  waves of dinosaurs that pour out of huge  portals floating in the sky in our  preview of the game last summer Phil  hornshaw wrote quote though we played  only a few hours and saw only a small  portion of what exoprimo has to offer  overall the game was surprisingly fun in  this technical test developer capcom's  approach to team-based gameplay uses a  lot of tried and true ideas borrowed  from other games to great effect and  fighting huge dinosaurs is just as cool  and pulse pounding as it sounds payday 3  is the long anticipated sequel to the  hit 2013 game Payday 2 and it was first  announced announced in 2016. the game  will take place in New York and will  feature the return of the original gang  from Payday 1. it will be available on  PC as well as Xbox and Playstation but  the developer didn't specify if that  means current gen last gen or both aside  from that there aren't any details  available for the game and the release  date is just as vague as the console  information and simply says 2023. if you  need a heist game sooner that isn't GTA  related then you might be interested in  Crime Boss Rock a city which releases on  March 28th Crime Boss is a first person  shooter with a star-studded cast that  includes Michael Matson Danny Trejo  Vanilla Ice and Chuck freaking Norris  just to name a few the gameplay reveal  trailer released in December 2022  focused on a co-op heist mission and  showed off the game's stealth shotguns  and ARS as well as the members of the  crew getting knocked down and revived  publisher 505 games and developer  in-game Studio say that Crime Boss  Rakesh City will feature a roguelike  campaign Sheriff Norris of course played  by Chuck Norris will be attempting to  stop players along with gang overlords  like one played by Vanilla Ice looking  for more of an old school feeling game  keep your eyes peeled for Warhammer 40  000 bolt gun in this 90s style retro  shooter you play as a Space Marine on a  mission across the Galaxy to defeat  chaos based Marines the game features  stylish visuals and based on the trailer  a kick-ass metal soundtrack on the more  modern side of things is Warhammer 40  000 Space Marine 2. this third person  action shooter is also slated for a 2023  release and sees you playing as you  guessed it a Space Marine some other  notable titles include RoboCop Rogue  City a first person shooter in which you  uphold the law in the crime riddled  streets of old Detroit wanted Dead a  hybrid shooter slasher from the makers  of Ninja Gaiden and dead or alive 5 the  finals a free-to-play first-person  shooter with destructible Arenas are  creators a free-to-play third-person  Co-op shooter that has you fighting  waves of mechanized enemies and my  favorite anger foot a fast-paced first  person shooter about kicking ass to  Kick-Ass beats which of these games are  you most excited to play let us know in  the comments  [Music]

